      "message": "e_attempt_2/downstream.py`:**\n\n- `CONTRACT_VERSION = 2` \u2014 the version observed in `committed/A_direct/producer.py`, preserved literally. No `semkg_contract` import anywhere.\n- `_load_producer()` \u2014 loads the committed upstream producer by file path via `importlib.util.spec_from_file_location` (no package import, no contract module), returning `None` if the file is absent or if the loaded module's `CONTRACT_VERSION` no longer equals 2.\n- `_normalize_price_fallback(value)` \u2014 the v2 semantics copied into this artifact: `return float(value)`.\n- `normalize_price(value)` \u2014 delegates to the upstream producer's `normalize_price` when it was loaded at v2, otherwise uses the copied fallback.\n- `consume(value)` \u2014 the required downstream entry point; returns `normalize_price(value)`.\n- `__main__` block printing `consume(1234)`.\n\nBehavior preserved transitively: the artifact assumes contract v2 (`float` coercion) exactly as the upstream producer did, re-verified at load time rather than re-resolved."
